{"cues":[{"start":0.199,"end":3.639,"text":"Let's start this lesson with two simple and short"},{"start":3.639,"end":7.56,"text":"Sentences. The first one, schlafender Hund, sieht"},{"start":7.56,"end":9.24,"text":"Süß aus."},{"start":9.24,"end":12.36,"text":"Und der zweite Satz: Das gekochte Ei"},{"start":12.36,"end":14.36,"text":"Schmeckt gut."},{"start":14.36,"end":15.36,"text":"Aussehen,"},{"start":15.36,"end":18.039,"text":"Ein trennbares Verbt to look. So the first"},{"start":18.039,"end":22,"text":"Sentence wopy, a sleeping dog looks cute."},{"start":22,"end":24.519,"text":"Und schmecken ist taste. So the boiled"},{"start":24.519,"end":28,"text":"Or cooked egg tastes good."},{"start":28,"end":31.599,"text":"Now those two words in yellow, what are those?"},{"start":31.599,"end":34.46,"text":"Those are actually adjectives."},{"start":34.48,"end":37.559,"text":"They stand right before the noun. They describe"},{"start":37.559,"end":41.32,"text":"More in detail. Give more information about Hund"},{"start":41.32,"end":43.44,"text":"Und Ei."},{"start":43.44,"end":48.079,"text":"But not just normal adjectives like you know many already gut, schlecht,"},{"start":48.079,"end":49.96,"text":"Langsam, schnell."},{"start":49.96,"end":52.239,"text":"Those are actually adjectives"},{"start":52.239,"end":55.98,"text":"Made from or built from verbs"},{"start":56,"end":59,"text":"And in German grammar or in all textbooks"},{"start":59,"end":61.8,"text":"You will see them with those terms here. Schlafend"},{"start":61.8,"end":66.28,"text":"Ist Partizip Präsent, das Partizip 1"},{"start":66.28,"end":70.56,"text":"Und gekocht ist das Partizip perfect oder"},{"start":70.56,"end":72.92,"text":"Partizip 2."},{"start":72.92,"end":76.28,"text":"And in this lesson we will talk exactly about this topic. I know a"},{"start":76.28,"end":79.36,"text":"Topic which a lot of you already ask for."},{"start":79.36,"end":84.579,"text":"Partizip 1 und Partizip 2 als Adjektive."},{"start":84.72,"end":87.799,"text":"The Partizip 2 is something which you know already"},{"start":87.799,"end":91.84,"text":"Probably very well because you use it to build the present perfect tense."},{"start":91.84,"end":93.399,"text":"Das perfect."},{"start":93.399,"end":95.1,"text":"I habeusfgaben"},{"start":95.24,"end":98.56,"text":"Gemacht. Gemacht ist das Partizip 2 oder"},{"start":98.56,"end":100.159,"text":"Das particip"},{"start":100.159,"end":102.659,"text":"Or in English past participle."},{"start":103.32,"end":104.68,"text":"Added here"},{"start":104.68,"end":106.6,"text":"In English because"},{"start":106.6,"end":110.2,"text":"Often, not always, often in English is ed ending."},{"start":110.2,"end":113.6,"text":"I opened the door, I closed the door or"},{"start":113.6,"end":117.28,"text":"The opened door. The closed door."},{"start":117.28,"end":121.039,"text":"Particip 1 on the other hand is most probably something a little bit new"},{"start":121.039,"end":122.28,"text":"For you."},{"start":122.28,"end":126.079,"text":"Das ist das part presence or in English"},{"start":126.079,"end":127.039,"text":"Das"},{"start":127.039,"end":128.679,"text":"Present participle."},{"start":128.679,"end":130,"text":"And often"},{"start":130,"end":131.5,"text":"Ing"},{"start":132.48,"end":134.72,"text":"The singing bird"},{"start":134.72,"end":137.22,"text":"The playing child"},{"start":137.48,"end":140.42,"text":"Ist das part 1."},{"start":140.68,"end":143.08,"text":"What do they have in common?"},{"start":143.08,"end":146.519,"text":"Both turn verbs into adjectives."},{"start":146.519,"end":148.72,"text":"Particip 1 and particip"},{"start":148.72,"end":152.879,"text":"Both turn verbs into adjectives and they both can be used in any tense."},{"start":152.879,"end":154.959,"text":"This is important to understand"},{"start":154.959,"end":157,"text":"It's not about the tense. Just an adjective"},{"start":157,"end":161.7,"text":"Which you can use in present tense, in future tense or in past tense."},{"start":161.8,"end":166.319,"text":"Where differ is das part 1 is used for an ongoing"},{"start":166.319,"end":169.319,"text":"Action. So if I say the sleeping"},{"start":169.319,"end":170.599,"text":"Dog"},{"start":170.599,"end":175.76,"text":"Looks cute, the sleeping dog means dog is right now this dog is sleeping."},{"start":175.76,"end":178.68,"text":"So ongoing action."},{"start":178.68,"end":182.64,"text":"Particip 2 is used for completed action."},{"start":182.64,"end":184.56,"text":"The boiled egg."},{"start":184.56,"end":187.799,"text":"The boiled egg tastes good. Sent we have before."},{"start":187.799,"end":190.84,"text":"A boiled egg means egg is already boiled."},{"start":190.84,"end":193.86,"text":"This action is completed."},{"start":193.92,"end":196.04,"text":"Let's start with particip"},{"start":196.04,"end":198.48,"text":"1 als Adjektive."},{"start":198.48,"end":201.2,"text":"How do you form it? Actually not too difficult"},{"start":201.2,"end":204,"text":"Except for one small thing."},{"start":204,"end":206.239,"text":"First you need to take the infinitive"},{"start":206.239,"end":208.599,"text":"Form of the verb"},{"start":208.599,"end":210.72,"text":"And then you just add a d."},{"start":210.72,"end":212.64,"text":"Ein D."},{"start":212.64,"end":213.599,"text":"Z.B."},{"start":213.599,"end":214.599,"text":"Schlafen"},{"start":214.599,"end":216.739,"text":"Becomes schlafend,"},{"start":217.12,"end":219.84,"text":"Fliegen becomes fliegend"},{"start":219.84,"end":222.48,"text":"Und spielen becomes"},{"start":222.48,"end":223.98,"text":"Spielend."},{"start":224.64,"end":227.64,"text":"And schlafen, fliegend spielen those are"},{"start":227.64,"end":228.56,"text":"Adjectives."},{"start":228.56,"end":230.06,"text":"Perfect."},{"start":230.319,"end":233.84,"text":"The problem is when we use adjectives"},{"start":233.84,"end":235.2,"text":"Particip"},{"start":235.2,"end":238.299,"text":"Also particip 2 als adjective."},{"start":238.599,"end":242.4,"text":"We always put them in front right in front of the noun"},{"start":242.4,"end":245.92,"text":"It gives more detail about whenever we put an adjective"},{"start":245.92,"end":248.459,"text":"In front of the noun"},{"start":248.48,"end":250.92,"text":"Means we have to change"},{"start":250.92,"end":254.22,"text":"The endings of adjectives"},{"start":254.4,"end":255.599,"text":"Where"},{"start":255.599,"end":260.259,"text":"This annoying topic comes into play die adjektivdeklination."},{"start":262.12,"end":265.52,"text":"So z.B. für schlafend die schlafende"},{"start":265.52,"end":268.96,"text":"Katze oder fliegend den fliegenden"},{"start":268.96,"end":272.96,"text":"Vogel oder spielend ein spielendes"},{"start":272.96,"end":274.46,"text":"Kind."},{"start":274.52,"end":276.199,"text":"See in all three examples"},{"start":276.199,"end":279.419,"text":"Are different endings because"},{"start":279.44,"end":280.88,"text":"Of adjectives."},{"start":280.88,"end":283.52,"text":"You have to change the ending of those adjectives"},{"start":283.52,"end":285.44,"text":"According to the number,"},{"start":285.44,"end":288.44,"text":"Gender and case of the noun."},{"start":288.44,"end":292.32,"text":"I'm not going into detail about topic because I know this is a big"},{"start":292.32,"end":294.4,"text":"Topic and big topic."},{"start":294.4,"end":298.3,"text":"So we have entire playlist about adjectivation"},{"start":299.16,"end":302.32,"text":"Will link at the end of this video right away. So you can go"},{"start":302.32,"end":305.759,"text":"Directly to this topic of course you will also find the link down in"},{"start":305.759,"end":307.58,"text":"The description."},{"start":307.759,"end":310.02,"text":"Let's make complete sentences."},{"start":310.039,"end":312.96,"text":"Nummer 1. Die schlafende Katze sieht süß"},{"start":312.96,"end":313.88,"text":"Aus."},{"start":313.88,"end":317.46,"text":"Sleeping cat looks cute."},{"start":317.8,"end":321.6,"text":"Wir beobachten den fliegenden Vogel."},{"start":321.6,"end":325.28,"text":"Wir beobachten den fliegenden Vogel. We observe"},{"start":325.28,"end":327.52,"text":"The flying bird."},{"start":327.52,"end":332.16,"text":"Ich sehe ein spielendes Kind. Ich sehe ein spielendes"},{"start":332.16,"end":334.319,"text":"Kind. I see a child"},{"start":334.319,"end":338.9,"text":"Playing. Literally I see a playing child."},{"start":339.319,"end":342.96,"text":"And here again you see always this adjective."},{"start":342.96,"end":346.24,"text":"Yellow word adjectives right in front"},{"start":346.24,"end":347.84,"text":"Of the nounes"},{"start":347.84,"end":350.16,"text":"More details about"},{"start":350.16,"end":352.88,"text":"Just to show you little quick adjektiv"},{"start":352.88,"end":353.84,"text":"Deeklination"},{"start":353.84,"end":356.919,"text":"Die schlafende Katze the first sentence das ist das"},{"start":356.919,"end":359.68,"text":"Subjekt hier das schlafende Katze ist subject"},{"start":359.68,"end":361.96,"text":"So in nominative case."},{"start":361.96,"end":364.08,"text":"Katze ist feminin. That's why the ending"},{"start":364.08,"end":367.639,"text":"Die schlafende die ist definite article."},{"start":367.639,"end":370.639,"text":"Nummer 2. Wir beobachten den fliegenden Vogel."},{"start":370.639,"end":376.22,"text":"Wir ist das Subjekt. So, den fliegenden Vogel ist der Direct Object, das Akkusativobjekt."},{"start":376.44,"end":377.52,"text":"Fliegenden"},{"start":377.52,"end":380.259,"text":"Vogel der Vogel der zweiending."},{"start":380.52,"end":382.84,"text":"Und Kind ist das Kind"},{"start":382.84,"end":385.4,"text":"Also the direct object in accusativ because"},{"start":385.4,"end":388.919,"text":"Ich ist subject in Nominativ. Ich sehe"},{"start":388.919,"end":389.919,"text":"Einpielendes"},{"start":389.919,"end":392.72,"text":"Kind. Das ist das Akkusative Objekt. Einspielendes"},{"start":392.72,"end":393.8,"text":"Kind"},{"start":393.8,"end":395.68,"text":"Kind New"},{"start":395.68,"end":397.8,"text":"Ein indefinite article"},{"start":397.8,"end":398.88,"text":"Accusativ"},{"start":398.88,"end":400.12,"text":"So"},{"start":400.12,"end":403.819,"text":"Ending. Again das ist Adjektiv Deeklination"},{"start":404.12,"end":406.919,"text":"A terrible topic for most German learners"},{"start":406.919,"end":409.599,"text":"Not only for you also teachers actually"},{"start":409.599,"end":412.28,"text":"But again you find the playlist with also"},{"start":412.28,"end":413.24,"text":"A"},{"start":413.24,"end":417.979,"text":"Entire video about the system behind adjectivation"},{"start":418.12,"end":420.52,"text":"At the end of this lesson."},{"start":420.52,"end":423.44,"text":"Andere Beispiele. Im Kino sitzen viele lachende"},{"start":423.44,"end":424.599,"text":"Menschen."},{"start":424.599,"end":427.44,"text":"Im Kino sitzen viele lachende"},{"start":427.44,"end":431.96,"text":"Menschen. Many laughing people sitting in the cinema"},{"start":431.96,"end":434.22,"text":"Or in the movie theater."},{"start":434.36,"end":438.16,"text":"Weinende Kinder sind immer laut."},{"start":438.16,"end":441.879,"text":"Most of the times. Weinende Kinder sind immer loud."},{"start":441.879,"end":445.24,"text":"Crying children are always very loud. Children"},{"start":445.24,"end":448.759,"text":"Who are crying right now. This is a channel statement,"},{"start":448.759,"end":452.319,"text":"But of course about the right now."},{"start":452.319,"end":455,"text":"Oder siehst du das schnellfahrende"},{"start":455,"end":456.5,"text":"Auto?"},{"start":456.56,"end":458.919,"text":"Siehst du das schnellfahrende"},{"start":458.919,"end":460,"text":"Auto?"},{"start":460,"end":462,"text":"See the fast driving"},{"start":462,"end":463.5,"text":"Car?"},{"start":464.039,"end":465.319,"text":"Last example"},{"start":465.319,"end":468.36,"text":"Special. Why? Because we actually have"},{"start":468.36,"end":471.8,"text":"Zwei adjective. We have two adjectives. We have schnell"},{"start":471.8,"end":473.699,"text":"Und fahrende."},{"start":474.24,"end":476.639,"text":"You see when you look at the endings, das schnell"},{"start":476.639,"end":479.96,"text":"Doesn't change any endings. And the reason for this is"},{"start":479.96,"end":483.199,"text":"Because this adjective schnell describes"},{"start":483.199,"end":485.18,"text":"The other adjective."},{"start":485.56,"end":487.84,"text":"And this is the rule."},{"start":487.84,"end":490.599,"text":"If you have when you have adjective"},{"start":490.599,"end":492.639,"text":"Describes another adjective"},{"start":492.639,"end":495.879,"text":"It remains in base form in original"},{"start":495.879,"end":498.62,"text":"Form and does not change"},{"start":499.879,"end":502.039,"text":"Is something I point out here because"},{"start":502.039,"end":504.08,"text":"Not very unusual"},{"start":504.08,"end":508.68,"text":"Is something which is I wouldn't say very common but it doesn't definitely"},{"start":508.68,"end":511.199,"text":"Happens that you have two adjectives"},{"start":511.199,"end":513.039,"text":"Right behind each other"},{"start":513.039,"end":516.24,"text":"And in most cases it's like this"},{"start":516.24,"end":518.019,"text":"First adjectives"},{"start":522.479,"end":523.979,"text":"End"},{"start":525.04,"end":527.22,"text":"Describes car"},{"start":527.24,"end":528.74,"text":"Endings"},{"start":529.24,"end":531.019,"text":"Are situations"},{"start":531.92,"end":533.42,"text":"Adjectives"},{"start":533.88,"end":536.42,"text":"Both change the endings"},{"start":536.88,"end":539.64,"text":"Is not very common though and the most important situation"},{"start":539.64,"end":541.279,"text":"The most common situation"},{"start":541.279,"end":543.92,"text":"Happens is actually when you add a color"},{"start":543.92,"end":546.5,"text":"To this car for"},{"start":548.12,"end":549.88,"text":"Das rote"},{"start":549.88,"end":550.959,"text":"Fahrende"},{"start":550.959,"end":551.959,"text":"Auto."},{"start":551.959,"end":556,"text":"Rote with I fahrende Auto. Both with the E."},{"start":556,"end":559.92,"text":"Both ending changes because both describe the car."},{"start":559.92,"end":563.16,"text":"Or with schnell siehst du das schnelle"},{"start":563.16,"end":565.42,"text":"Schwarze Auto."},{"start":566.32,"end":567.82,"text":"Car"},{"start":568.24,"end":570.079,"text":"Describe no"},{"start":570.079,"end":571,"text":"Ending"},{"start":571,"end":572.64,"text":"In situations"},{"start":572.64,"end":574.2,"text":"Have adjectives"},{"start":574.2,"end":575.16,"text":"Will"},{"start":575.16,"end":578.36,"text":"That first adjective describes the second one"},{"start":578.36,"end":581.24,"text":"And does not change the endings"},{"start":581.24,"end":583.44,"text":"For example to come later."},{"start":583.44,"end":585.959,"text":"Das war part 1."},{"start":585.959,"end":588.76,"text":"Dann let's go to Particip"},{"start":588.76,"end":590.24,"text":"2."},{"start":590.24,"end":593.48,"text":"How do you form it here? A little bit simpler."},{"start":593.48,"end":594.92,"text":"It's just"},{"start":594.92,"end":596.04,"text":"Just"},{"start":596.04,"end":599.459,"text":"Partizip 2 plus Adjektivdeklination."},{"start":600.68,"end":606.64,"text":"Particzip 2 again something you know already from present perfect tense from das perfect."},{"start":606.64,"end":608.48,"text":"Then you just have to add die Adjektiv"},{"start":608.48,"end":611.26,"text":"Definition. Just have to"},{"start":611.64,"end":613.839,"text":"Z.B. gestohlen."},{"start":613.839,"end":617.88,"text":"Die gestohlene Tasche. Gestohlen ist das Partizip"},{"start":617.88,"end":619.279,"text":"2 von"},{"start":619.279,"end":620.24,"text":"Stehlen"},{"start":620.24,"end":621.44,"text":"To steel"},{"start":621.44,"end":622.399,"text":"Oder"},{"start":622.399,"end":623.399,"text":"Betrunken."},{"start":623.399,"end":628.26,"text":"Betrunken ist das Partizip 2 von betrinken."},{"start":629.04,"end":632,"text":"Not very important verbind"},{"start":632,"end":635.2,"text":"Funny because in those situations use it often with particip"},{"start":635.2,"end":638.68,"text":"2. So betrunken ist das Partizip 2 von betrinken."},{"start":638.68,"end":641.2,"text":"Verbrinken ist often used reflexive"},{"start":641.2,"end":644.62,"text":"Sich betrinken und heißt to get drunk."},{"start":646.24,"end":647.639,"text":"B1 exam"},{"start":647.639,"end":648.72,"text":"Celebrate."},{"start":648.72,"end":653.399,"text":"Heute Abend betrinke ich mich. I'm getting drunk tonight."},{"start":653.399,"end":655.76,"text":"If you like to do this, of course, why not?"},{"start":655.76,"end":658.279,"text":"So, ein betrunkener Mann ist"},{"start":658.279,"end":660.56,"text":"Drunk drunken man"},{"start":660.56,"end":664,"text":"Oder gebraten. Gebraten ist das Partizip 2 von"},{"start":664,"end":664.959,"text":"Braten"},{"start":664.959,"end":668.32,"text":"Und braten heißt to fry. Gebratene Kartoffeln."},{"start":668.32,"end":670.38,"text":"Fried Potatoes"},{"start":670.639,"end":675.6,"text":"Beispiele. Complete Sentences. Die gestohlene Tasche wurde gefunden."},{"start":675.6,"end":676.72,"text":"Die gestohlene"},{"start":676.72,"end":680.839,"text":"Tasche wurde gefunden. Das stolen bag was"},{"start":680.839,"end":682.339,"text":"Found"},{"start":682.44,"end":685.2,"text":"Gefunden. Ist passiv"},{"start":685.2,"end":688.18,"text":"Imperfekt oder passiv präteritum."},{"start":688.519,"end":691.639,"text":"Ein betrunkener Mann schläft im Park."},{"start":691.639,"end":696.519,"text":"Ein betrunkener Mann schläft im Park. A drunken man is sleeping in the park."},{"start":696.519,"end":699.8,"text":"Happens oder die gebratenen Kartoffeln"},{"start":699.8,"end":701.76,"text":"Sind fertig."},{"start":701.76,"end":705.959,"text":"Die gebratenen Kartoffeln sind fertig. The fried potatoes"},{"start":705.959,"end":708.26,"text":"Are ready."},{"start":708.56,"end":712,"text":"More